  "summary": "Eleven preprints and three published papers apply ML to single-cell and regulatory genomics prediction; none explicitly address diabetes or pathways.",
  "synthesis": "The items cluster around deep learning for single-cell and regulatory genomics. Preprints include CLAMP, which learns interpretable gene modules from 605,614 ARCHS4 RNA-seq samples; an evaluation of AlphaGenome against Enformer for personal, tissue-specific expression prediction; and several virtual-cell efforts, including MultiFlow, Scooby-2, and a centered perturbation-transfer method scoring 0.341 on the 2025 Virtual Cell Challenge benchmark. Reliability transfer in single-cell foundation models is examined separately from prediction transfer across ten systems. Published work spans chromatin accessibility (XChrom), chromatin interaction prediction (UniLoopNet), and cell-death regulator nomination (xNNPCD). The rise ratio of 2.8 describes observed activity across these 14 items; the items do not establish why activity is increasing, and no code, industry, or star-gain signals are recorded. The pathway-diabetic label is not reflected in the item texts.",
